{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1517296-new-age-sorcery-birth-of-obsidian-cows-\ud83e\udd5b","id":1517296,"title":"New Age Sorcery: Birth of Obsidian Cows \ud83e\udd5b","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-06T11:46:28-07:00","id":1517296,"title":"New Age Sorcery: Birth of Obsidian Cows \ud83e\udd5b","content":"<div align=\"center\"><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/964950922910376026/1126581404034146324/IMG_0834.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/964950922910376026/1126581404034146324/IMG_0834.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://media.discordapp.net/attachments/964950922910376026/1126581404034146324/IMG_0834.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> <br /> So now that it\u2019ll be possible to add more charms to a MA through secret technique, that just leave Sorcery as the most rigid and \u201cundeveloped\u201d power space amongst the 4 (Charm, Evocation, MA, Spell), as in where do you even start when you want to create a new Spell? Do you have to research phenomenon to base your spell on? Or\u2026. I actually can\u2019t even think of any more examples since I don\u2019t think any book has ever talked about this! Like, Total Annihilation is base on Ligier, does the spell creator just channel sorcerous essence in a specific way to invent the spell? Or maybe ask Ligier for permission to invent the spell???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T12:43:33-07:00","id":1517300,"title":"","content":"They probably studied Liger's powers in use - manageable when he's just a green sun hanging in the sky, slightly more risky when he's hucking stuff at you on the battlefield. If he gave permission and helped out (probably well after the war, if he made a friends or something), more the better. It's mostly a matter of analyzing a phenomenon or cosmological constant, and figuring out how the Essence flows Weave together.<br /> <br /> So in this case, the &quot;Friendship Beam&quot; could potentially be a remnant of Aurora-Who-Was. Meaning the Sorcerer would either need to study Remembrance, Veiled In Light, talk with veterans of the Primordial War, and/or learn it as a &quot;forgotten&quot; spell from the only remaining practitioner(s)/written record.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value"